title: Enforce the law
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_catalonia
view-if: catalan_crisis = 1 and cat_155_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; cat_155_timer = 3

= Enforce the law

The Constitutional Court's rulings are being ignored. How far should the State go?

- @prosecute: Back the prosecution of the independence leaders
- @police: Reinforce the police in Catalonia
- @measured: Act, but with the minimum force the law allows
- @easy_discard

@prosecute
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_hard_line += 1; Q.rel_erc -= 12; Q.rel_junts -= 12; Q.rel_cs += 4; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 6; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.territorial(Q, 'Cataluña', 'erc', 1.05); window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'psoe', {pensioners: 1}); } !}

The rule of law, applied fully. The independence movement now has martyrs.

@police
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_hard_line += 1; Q.rel_erc -= 8; Q.rel_up -= 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.campaign(Q, 'vox', {pensioners: -0.5, self_employed: -0.5}); } !}

The State shows it is present. Vox has less to shout about, for now.

@measured
on-arrival: cat_dialogue += 1; regional_leaders_dissent += 3; rel_erc += 2

Firm but proportionate, says the government. Too soft, says the right; too hard, say the separatists.

@dialogue
title: A table for dialogue
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_catalonia
view-if: catalan_crisis = 1 and cat_dialogue_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; cat_dialogue_timer = 3

= A table for dialogue

The PSC proposes a table where the two governments can talk, without preconditions and without a referendum.

- @propose: Propose the table publicly
- @mediator: Accept an international mediator
- @no_talks: No talks while the law is being broken
- @easy_discard

@propose
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_dialogue += 1; Q.rel_erc += 8; Q.rel_junts += 5; Q.rel_cs -= 8; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 8; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 1); } !}

ERC is interested. Ciudadanos calls it treason; García-Page calls it naive.

@mediator
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_dialogue += 2; Q.rel_erc += 10; Q.rel_junts += 10; Q.rel_cs -= 15; Q.rel_pp -= 10; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 18; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 10; Q.sanchez_authority -= 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 2); } !}

Puigdemont's people are delighted. Within the PSOE, it is a scandal.

@no_talks
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_hard_line += 1; Q.rel_erc -= 8; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 5; Q.rel_cs += 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, -0.5); } !}

Clear and firm. And the conflict goes on.

@psc
title: The PSC line
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_catalonia
view-if: catalan_crisis = 1 and cat_psc_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; cat_psc_timer = 3

= The PSC line

Miquel Iceta needs to win back voters who fled to Ciudadanos without losing those who want a deal. What does the PSOE let him say?

- @iceta_bridge: A bridge: recognise Catalonia as a nation within Spain
- @iceta_unionist: A clear unionist line, shoulder to shoulder with Cs
- @iceta_free: Let the PSC set its own line
- @easy_discard

@iceta_bridge
on-arrival: {! Q.cat_dialogue += 1; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 6; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 1.06); } if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 1); } !}

Iceta dances on stage and talks about a "nation of nations". Some voters come back.

@iceta_unionist
on-arrival: {! Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 1.03); window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'cs', 1.03); } !}

The PSC competes with Ciudadanos on its own ground, and Ciudadanos is better at it.

@iceta_free
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority -= 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.regionalMod(Q, 'Cataluña', 'psoe', 1.04); } !}

The PSC is its own party, after all. Madrid hopes it knows what it is doing.

@federal_reform
title: A federal answer
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_catalonia
view-if: catalan_crisis = 1 and cat_federal_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; cat_federal_timer = 6

= A federal answer

The Granada Declaration of 2013 proposed a federal Spain. Is now the moment to put it on the table?

- @propose_reform: Propose a constitutional reform commission
- @not_now: Not now: first restore the law
- @easy_discard

@propose_reform
on-arrival: {! Q.federal_proposal = 1; Q.constitutional_commission = 1; Q.cat_dialogue += 1; Q.rel_pnv += 6; Q.rel_erc += 4; Q.rel_pp -= 4; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 4; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 2; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 0.8); } !}

The PP agrees to a commission and to nothing else. It is a start.

@not_now
on-arrival: {! Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 4; Q.rel_pnv -= 3; Q.cat_hard_line += 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, -0.3); } !}

The reform can wait. The question is whether the conflict will.
